#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
held-tool-watch — a SENSOR for a tool call that has been pending a while, seen from OUTSIDE its
session. It senses, calls and says; it never judges, approves, cancels, retries or signals a session.

On 2026-11-23 a coordinating session's tool call sat pending for about seven hours (very likely an
approval prompt nobody saw), and another for 45 minutes, while the device kept exchanging. Nothing
told the steward, the sibling device or `berth status`. This script reads the transcripts the harness
already writes and hands what it senses to the native fold.

  held-tool-watch scan    [--transcripts DIR] [--sense-after-s 120] [--now UNIX] [--json]
                          [--sessions-json FILE] [--stasis-root DIR] [--tail-bytes N]
      Read only. Candidates out; exit 0 when none, 3 when some.
  held-tool-watch observe [same flags] [--bin-store DIR]
      One pass, then exit. For each candidate, call
        <the TARGET session's pinned epr> session stasis observe --session S --source watcher:held-tool
            --tool T --pending-since <RFC3339 of the pending tool_use> [--agent A] --journal-root R
      Exit 0 when the pass ran (whether it observed, skipped or found nothing); 1 on any internal
      error or a failed observe call, with one line on stderr each. Never 2: a hook exit 2 blocks the
      tool call it runs beside, and this script must never raise into one.
  held-tool-watch announce [same flags] [--bin-store DIR]
      `observe`, then make it visible, once: for each observed call whose session's native status
      (read through the same pinned epr) has an open incident, `berth say --session held-tool-watch
      --to <each live session moored here or on a sibling device, the held one excepted>` one line
      `held-tool@1 open k=<key> ...` (the household when no session is listed); for each call announced
      earlier whose transcript now holds its result (or is gone), one line `held-tool@1 resumed k=...`
      to the same addressees. Same exit contract as `observe`.
  held-tool-watch run [same flags] [--bin-store DIR] [--every 60] [--passes N]
      The device runner: one per device (a lock beside the stasis root), an `announce` pass in a fresh
      process every --every seconds, the last pass's output in `held-tool-watch.last-pass.txt` there.

Thresholds. `--sense-after-s` (default 120) is the only one: the sensor reports a call pending longer
than that. It judges nothing else; the native Incident records the interval and `elohim_epr_rea::Bound`
judges its age. Pending is NOT sensed when the tool is long-running by design: Agent / Task /
Workflow / Monitor / TaskOutput; Bash with `run_in_background: true`; Bash with an explicit
`timeout` until that timeout plus a 30 s grace. A killed subagent whose last line is a tool_use looks
the same as a held one. `cause` (scan only) is `approval-evidence` when a `permission-requested` entry
in the dialogue-stasis journal names the tool_use id as its `precedingToolUseId`; otherwise `unknown`.

No state of its own. `--pending-since` is the pending tool_use's own transcript timestamp, so observing
the same call on every run names the same (session, agent, tool, pending-since), and the native side
folds those repeats into one incident. `announce` hashes that same key into `k=`, and "once" is read
from the record the saying makes: the notes this watcher said, as folded in this device's channel
store (`berth said --session held-tool-watch`), which is also what crosses to the siblings. A line is
said to an addressee only when no line of that kind and key to that addressee is in the record; if the
record cannot be read, nothing is said that pass. A note that did not reach the store (`berth say`
exit 1) is said again next pass. The script keeps no marker or announce-once file; the two lock files
order writers and record nothing. Held state is the native Incident: nothing is announced unless the
target's own epr shows an open incident, and `berth status` renders `held` from that same read.
Resumption is read from the transcript (the call's result appears), because no native verb lets an
outside observer record it: the native Silence incident closes at that agent's next turn end.

Compatibility (the hazard this design answers). A session keeps the epr build it was pinned to when
it started, and an epr older than `observe` rejects the unknown event kind `tool-pending-observed`
and aborts replay of that session's stasis journal. This script writes into ANOTHER session's
journal, so it writes ONLY through the TARGET session's own pinned epr: the writer is then never newer
than that session's reader. On this device a session's pin is the JSON file
`<bin-store>/epr/sessions/<session id>` ({"cid", "session", ...}, the key encoded as
device-runtime's `Store::pin_path` encodes it) and its binary is `<bin-store>/epr/<cid>/epr`; the
bin-store root comes from `--bin-store`, else from the path the native `epr bin resolve --tool epr
--json` prints (`<root>/epr/<cid>/epr`), so the native layout decides it, not this script. Before
writing, the pinned binary's `session stasis --help` must list `stasis observe`.
  - pinned epr lacks the verb: nothing written; one line
    `held-tool-watch: session <id> runs an epr without stasis observe; not observed`.
  - pin cannot be determined (no store, no pin file, a pin naming another session or a malformed
    CID, a missing binary): nothing written; one line saying why.
  - the session has no stasis journal (observe exits 2): nothing was written; one line.
A residual this does not cover: a reader of ALL sessions' journals (`epr session stasis status`
with no `--session`, as `berth status` runs it) under an older epr still meets the new kind in the
observed session's journal. That reader is the observer's device tooling, not the held session.

Registration (2026-11-25, the steward's direction "stop waiting and work on it"): the hook
`held-tool-ensure` (PostToolUse and SessionStart in Claude Code, PostToolUse and SessionStart in Codex)
starts `held-tool-watch run` detached when this device has no runner, in a few milliseconds and never
more. A held session fires no hooks, so the runner, not any hook, does the sensing: a device with one
session is covered from that session's first tool call, until the workspace restarts. Not covered: a
device where no session has started since its last restart; Codex sessions (their transcripts are
not read, only Claude Code's). The runner is not supervised by the device's ark: `epr device run`
declares only bin-store tools, and this script is not one.
"""
import argparse
import contextlib
import datetime
import fcntl
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time

LONG_RUNNING_TOOLS = {"Agent", "Task", "Workflow", "Monitor", "TaskOutput"}
TIMEOUT_GRACE_S = 30
SHAPE_CHARS = 80
DEFAULT_TAIL_BYTES = 8 * 1024 * 1024
HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
REPO_ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(HERE)))


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- locations

def main_checkout(root):
    """A linked worktree's main checkout (as berth finds it), else root."""
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(root, ".git")) as f:
            marker = f.read().strip()
        if not marker.startswith("gitdir: "):
            return root
        git_dir = os.path.realpath(os.path.join(root, marker[8:]))
        with open(os.path.join(git_dir, "commondir")) as f:
            common = os.path.realpath(os.path.join(git_dir, f.read().strip()))
        if os.path.basename(common) == ".git" and os.path.isdir(common):
            return os.path.dirname(common)
    except OSError:
        pass
    return root


def stasis_root():
    return os.path.join(main_checkout(REPO_ROOT), ".eprfs", "status", "stasis")


def transcripts_root():
    config = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR")
    if config:
        return os.path.join(config, "projects")
    if os.path.isdir("/projects/.claude-config/projects"):
        return "/projects/.claude-config/projects"
    return os.path.expanduser("~/.claude/projects")


def berth_bin():
    return os.environ.get("BERTH_BIN") or os.path.join(HERE, "berth")


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- redaction

_MASK = "<masked>"
_SECRET_PATTERNS = [
    (re.compile(r"(?i)(authorization:\s*)(bearer\s+|basic\s+|token\s+)?\S+"), r"\1" + _MASK),
    (re.compile(r"(?i)\bbearer\s+\S+"), "bearer " + _MASK),
    (re.compile(r"(?i)(\b[\w.-]*(?:token|key|secret|passw(?:or)?d|pwd|auth|credential)[\w.-]*\s*[=:]\s*)(\"[^\"]*\"|'[^']*'|\S+)"),
     r"\1" + _MASK),
    (re.compile(r"(?i)(--?[\w-]*(?:token|key|secret|passw(?:or)?d|auth)[\w-]*[ =])(\"[^\"]*\"|'[^']*'|\S+)"),
     r"\1" + _MASK),
    (re.compile(r"(\w+://[^\s/:@]+:)[^\s/@]+@"), r"\1" + _MASK + "@"),
    (re.compile(r"\?[^\s'\"]+"), "?" + _MASK),
    (re.compile(r"\b(?:ghp_|gho_|ghs_|github_pat_|sk-|xox[abpr]-|AKIA|eyJ)[A-Za-z0-9_\-.]{8,}"), _MASK),
    (re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9+/_\-]{32,}={0,2}"), _MASK),
]


def redact(text):
    """The first SHAPE_CHARS characters of a command, with token-, key-, password-, URL-query-like
    strings masked FIRST (so a secret straddling the cut cannot survive half-shown)."""
    text = " ".join(str(text).split())
    for pattern, replacement in _SECRET_PATTERNS:
        text = pattern.sub(replacement, text)
    return text[:SHAPE_CHARS]


def shape_of(tool, inputs):
    if not isinstance(inputs, dict):
        return "<opaque input>"
    if tool == "Bash":
        return redact(inputs.get("command", ""))
    for field in ("file_path", "path", "pattern", "url", "query"):
        if isinstance(inputs.get(field), str):
            return redact(inputs[field])
    return "<" + tool + ">"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- transcripts

def parse_ts(value):
    if not isinstance(value, str):
        return None
    try:
        return datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace("Z", "+00:00")).timestamp()
    except ValueError:
        return None


def read_lines(path, tail_bytes):
    """Complete lines of the file's last tail_bytes (a seek lands mid-line: that first line is dropped).
    A final line without a newline may be mid-write: it is returned and the parser skips it if it is
    not whole JSON; any other line that is not a JSON object makes the transcript malformed."""
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as f:
            size = f.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)
            start = max(0, size - tail_bytes) if tail_bytes else 0
            f.seek(start)
            data = f.read()
    except OSError:
        return []
    lines = data.split(b"\n")
    if start:
        lines = lines[1:]
    return lines


def dangling_calls(path, tail_bytes=DEFAULT_TAIL_BYTES):
    """tool_use blocks in the transcript with no tool_result of the same id, oldest first. A line that
    is not a JSON object anywhere but last raises ValueError: the sensor cannot say what it missed."""
    uses, results = {}, set()
    lines = read_lines(path, tail_bytes)
    for number, raw in enumerate(lines):
        if not raw.strip():
            continue
        try:
            row = json.loads(raw)
        except (ValueError, UnicodeDecodeError):
            row = None
        if not isinstance(row, dict):
            if number == len(lines) - 1:
                continue  # the last line may be mid-write
            raise ValueError(f"malformed transcript {path}: a non-final line is not a JSON object")
        message = row.get("message")
        blocks = message.get("content") if isinstance(message, dict) else None
        if not isinstance(blocks, list):
            continue
        for block in blocks:
            if not isinstance(block, dict):
                continue
            kind = block.get("type")
            if kind == "tool_result" and isinstance(block.get("tool_use_id"), str):
                results.add(block["tool_use_id"])
            elif kind == "tool_use" and isinstance(block.get("id"), str):
                when = parse_ts(row.get("timestamp"))
                if when is not None and block["id"] not in uses:
                    uses[block["id"]] = dict(id=block["id"], tool=str(block.get("name", "unknown")),
                                             input=block.get("input"), at=when)
    return sorted((u for i, u in uses.items() if i not in results), key=lambda u: u["at"])


def long_running_limit(tool, inputs, sense_after_s):
    """Seconds a pending call may age before it counts as held, or None when it is never held."""
    if tool in LONG_RUNNING_TOOLS:
        return None
    inputs = inputs if isinstance(inputs, dict) else {}
    if tool == "Bash":
        if inputs.get("run_in_background") is True:
            return None
        timeout = inputs.get("timeout")
        if isinstance(timeout, (int, float)) and not isinstance(timeout, bool) and timeout > 0:
            return max(sense_after_s, timeout / 1000 + TIMEOUT_GRACE_S)
    return sense_after_s


def find_transcripts(root, session):
    """[(agent, path)]: the main transcript wherever a project directory holds it, and each subagent's."""
    found = []
    if not os.path.isdir(root):
        return found
    for project in sorted(os.listdir(root)):
        main = os.path.join(root, project, session + ".jsonl")
        if os.path.isfile(main):
            found.append(("main", main))
            sub = os.path.join(root, project, session, "subagents")
            if os.path.isdir(sub):
                for name in sorted(os.listdir(sub)):
                    if name.startswith("agent-") and name.endswith(".jsonl"):
                        found.append((name[len("agent-"):-len(".jsonl")], os.path.join(sub, name)))
    return found


def approval_evidence(root, session):
    """tool_use ids a dialogue-stasis journal ties to a permission request."""
    ids = set()
    directory = os.path.join(root, session)
    try:
        names = sorted(n for n in os.listdir(directory) if n.startswith("events") and n.endswith(".jsonl"))
    except OSError:
        return ids
    for name in names:
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(directory, name), "rb") as f:
                for raw in f:
                    try:
                        row = json.loads(raw)
                    except (ValueError, UnicodeDecodeError):
                        continue
                    if isinstance(row, dict) and row.get("kind") == "permission-requested":
                        source = row.get("source")
                        tool_id = source.get("precedingToolUseId") if isinstance(source, dict) else None
                        if isinstance(tool_id, str) and tool_id:
                            ids.add(tool_id)
        except OSError:
            continue
    return ids


def moored_sessions(sessions_json=None):
    """Session ids moored on this device, from `berth status --json --no-peer` (or an injected file)."""
    if sessions_json:
        with open(sessions_json) as f:
            data = json.load(f)
    else:
        out = subprocess.run([berth_bin(), "status", "--json", "--no-peer"], capture_output=True,
                             text=True, timeout=30, check=True)
        data = json.loads(out.stdout)
    rows = data.get("moorings", []) if isinstance(data, dict) else data
    return [r["session"] if isinstance(r, dict) else r for r in rows
            if (isinstance(r, dict) and isinstance(r.get("session"), str)) or isinstance(r, str)]


def scan(sessions, transcripts, sense_after_s, now, stasis=None, tail_bytes=DEFAULT_TAIL_BYTES):
    held = []
    for session in sessions:
        evidence = approval_evidence(stasis, session) if stasis else set()
        for agent, path in find_transcripts(transcripts, session):
            for call in dangling_calls(path, tail_bytes):
                limit = long_running_limit(call["tool"], call["input"], sense_after_s)
                age = now - call["at"]
                if limit is None or age <= limit:
                    continue
                held.append(dict(session=session, agent=agent, tool=call["tool"], toolUseId=call["id"],
                                 shape=shape_of(call["tool"], call["input"]), pendingS=int(age),
                                 calledAt=call["at"],
                                 cause="approval-evidence" if call["id"] in evidence else "unknown"))
    return held


def render_line(h):
    return (f"held  {h['session'][:8]}  {h['agent']}  {h['tool']}  {h['pendingS']}s  "
            f"cause: {h['cause']}  {h['shape']}")


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the target session's own epr

WATCHER_SOURCE = "watcher:held-tool"
NO_VERB_LINE = "held-tool-watch: session {session} runs an epr without stasis observe; not observed"
NO_PIN_LINE = "held-tool-watch: session {session} has no determinable epr pin ({why}); not observed"
NO_JOURNAL_LINE = "held-tool-watch: session {session} has no stasis journal; not observed"
_CID = re.compile(r"^baf[a-z2-7]{20,}$")


def run_command(argv, timeout=60):
    """(returncode, stdout, stderr). EPR_BIN is dropped so the named binary is the one that runs.
    The injectable runner's default."""
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k != "EPR_BIN"}
    out = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, env=env)
    return out.returncode, out.stdout, out.stderr


def pin_name(session):
    """device-runtime `Store::pin_path`'s file name for a session key, or None when it would hash."""
    name = "".join(chr(b) if (chr(b).isascii() and chr(b).isalnum()) or chr(b) in "_.-" else f"%{b:02x}"
                   for b in session.encode())
    if not name or len(name) > 200:
        return None
    return name.replace(".", "%2e") if name in (".", "..") else name


def native_bin_store(runner=run_command):
    """The bin-store root, from the path the native `epr bin resolve --tool epr --json` prints."""
    code, out, _ = runner(["epr", "bin", "resolve", "--tool", "epr", "--json"])
    if code != 0:
        return None
    path = json.loads(out).get("path")
    if not isinstance(path, str):
        return None
    tool_dir = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(path))  # <root>/epr/<cid>/epr -> <root>/epr
    return os.path.dirname(tool_dir) if os.path.basename(tool_dir) == "epr" else None


def pinned_epr(session, bin_store):
    """(path to the session's pinned epr, None) or (None, why)."""
    if not bin_store:
        return None, "no bin-store"
    name = pin_name(session)
    if name is None:
        return None, "session key not encodable here"
    tool_dir = os.path.join(bin_store, "epr")
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(tool_dir, "sessions", name)) as f:
            pin = json.load(f)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None, "no pin file"
    except (OSError, ValueError) as error:
        return None, f"unreadable pin: {type(error).__name__}"
    if not isinstance(pin, dict) or pin.get("session") != session:
        return None, "pin names another session"
    cid = pin.get("cid")
    if not isinstance(cid, str) or not _CID.match(cid):
        return None, "pin has no valid cid"
    binary = os.path.join(tool_dir, cid, "epr")
    if not os.access(binary, os.X_OK):
        return None, f"pinned binary {cid[:16]}… absent"
    return binary, None


def has_observe(binary, runner=run_command):
    code, out, err = runner([binary, "session", "stasis", "--help"], timeout=20)
    return code == 0 and "stasis observe" in out + err


def observe_argv(h, journal_root):
    argv = ["session", "stasis", "observe", "--session", h["session"], "--source", WATCHER_SOURCE,
            "--tool", h["tool"], "--pending-since", rfc3339(h["calledAt"])]
    if h["agent"] != "main":
        argv += ["--agent", h["agent"]]
    return argv + ["--journal-root", journal_root]


def rfc3339(t):
    return datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(t, datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def observe_pass(held, journal_root, bin_store, runner=run_command, say=print, warn=None, observed=None):
    """Call each candidate's own session's pinned epr. Returns the number of failed calls; each
    candidate the native side recorded is appended to `observed` as (candidate, pinned binary)."""
    warn = warn or (lambda line: print(line, file=sys.stderr))
    failed, verbs = 0, {}
    for h in held:
        session = h["session"]
        binary, why = pinned_epr(session, bin_store)
        if binary is None:
            say(NO_PIN_LINE.format(session=session, why=why))
            continue
        if binary not in verbs:
            verbs[binary] = has_observe(binary, runner)
        if not verbs[binary]:
            say(NO_VERB_LINE.format(session=session))
            continue
        code, _, err = runner([binary] + observe_argv(h, journal_root))
        if code == 0:
            if observed is not None:
                observed.append((h, binary))
            continue
        if code == 2 and "no journal" in err:
            say(NO_JOURNAL_LINE.format(session=session))
            continue
        failed += 1
        detail = " ".join(err.split())[:160] or "no output"
        warn(f"held-tool-watch: observe for session {session} failed (exit {code}): {detail}")
    return failed


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- announcing, once, from the record

ANNOUNCER = "held-tool-watch"  # the berth sender of every line this watcher says
MARK = "held-tool@1"
ANNOUNCE_LOOKBACK_S = 7 * 86400  # an open line older than this is never followed by a resumed one
MAX_ADDRESSEES = 8
LOOP_LOCK = "held-tool-watch.run.lock"  # .claude/hooks/held-tool-ensure.py LOCK_NAME
ANNOUNCE_LOCK = "held-tool-watch.announce.lock"
LAST_PASS = "held-tool-watch.last-pass.txt"
_TOKEN = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:@+-]{0,199}$")
_FIELD = re.compile(r"(\w+)=(\S+)")


def berth_run(argv, runner):
    return runner([berth_bin()] + argv, timeout=60)


def token(value):
    """A value for the machine half of a line: shaped, or `?`."""
    value = str(value)
    return value if _TOKEN.match(value) else "?"


def announce_key(h):
    """The native incident key (session, agent, tool, pending-since), hashed. It names one held call on
    every pass, so the record of a line said for it is what makes the line once."""
    material = "\0".join([h["session"], h["agent"], h["tool"], rfc3339(h["calledAt"])])
    return hashlib.sha256(material.encode()).hexdigest()[:16]


def short_device(device):
    return f"{device[:16]}…{device[-4:]}" if device and len(device) > 24 else (device or "this device")


def clock(t):
    return datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(t, datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%H:%M")


def open_line(key, h, device, incident, now):
    minutes = max(1, int((now - h["calledAt"]) // 60))
    return (f"{MARK} open k={key} device={token(device or 'local')} session={token(h['session'])} "
            f"agent={token(h['agent'])} tool={token(h['tool'])} since={rfc3339(h['calledAt'])} "
            f"call={token(h['toolUseId'])} incident={token(incident)} — on {short_device(device)}, session "
            f"{h['session'][:8]} ({h['agent']}) has had a {h['tool']} call pending {minutes} min, since "
            f"{clock(h['calledAt'])}Z (cause: {h['cause']}; {h['shape']}): very likely a prompt nobody has "
            f"seen, and its terminal needs the steward. Nothing here approves, cancels or retries it; one "
            f"more line follows when it resumes.")


def resumed_line(key, f, now):
    since = parse_ts(f.get("since"))
    took = f"about {max(1, int((now - since) // 60))} min after it began" if since else "time unknown"
    return (f"{MARK} resumed k={key} device={f.get('device', '?')} session={f.get('session', '?')} "
            f"agent={f.get('agent', '?')} tool={f.get('tool', '?')} since={f.get('since', '?')} — the "
            f"{f.get('tool', '?')} call of session {f.get('session', '?')[:8]} ({f.get('agent', '?')}) on "
            f"{short_device(f.get('device'))} is no longer pending (answered, or its session ended), "
            f"{took}.")


def parse_mark(text):
    """(kind, fields) of a line this watcher said, else None."""
    if not isinstance(text, str) or not text.startswith(MARK + " "):
        return None
    head = text.split(" — ", 1)[0].split()
    if len(head) < 2:
        return None
    return head[1], dict(_FIELD.findall(" ".join(head[2:])))


def native_open_incidents(binary, session, journal_root, runner):
    """The ids of the session's open native incidents, read through ITS OWN pinned epr (so the reader is
    never older than what the writer wrote), or None when that read fails."""
    code, out, _ = runner([binary, "session", "stasis", "status", "--session", session, "--json",
                           "--journal-root", journal_root], timeout=30)
    if code != 0:
        return None
    try:
        data = json.loads(out)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    ids = []
    for row in data.get("sessions", []) if isinstance(data, dict) else []:
        if isinstance(row, dict) and row.get("session") == session:
            ids += [i["id"] for i in row.get("openIncidents") or []
                    if isinstance(i, dict) and isinstance(i.get("id"), str)]
    return ids


def addressees(status, held_session):
    """Every live session moored here or on a sibling device, other than the held one: the sessions
    whose next tool call (berth-note-inject) or Monitor shows an addressed note. None means the
    household, when no session is listed."""
    found = []
    for section in ("moorings", "siblings"):
        for row in status.get(section) or []:
            session = row.get("session") if isinstance(row, dict) else None
            if (isinstance(session, str) and _TOKEN.match(session) and session not in (held_session, ANNOUNCER)
                    and session not in found):
                found.append(session)
    return found[:MAX_ADDRESSEES] or [None]


def still_pending(transcripts, session, agent, call, tail_bytes=DEFAULT_TAIL_BYTES):
    """True while the call has no result in its transcript, False once it has one or the transcript is
    gone, None when the transcript cannot be read."""
    for name, path in find_transcripts(transcripts, session):
        if name == agent:
            try:
                return any(c["id"] == call for c in dangling_calls(path, tail_bytes))
            except ValueError:
                return None
    return False


def berth_json(argv, runner):
    code, out, err = berth_run(argv, runner)
    if code != 0:
        raise RuntimeError(f"berth {argv[0]} exited {code}: {' '.join(err.split())[:120] or 'no output'}")
    return json.loads(out)


def announce_pass(observed, journal_root, transcripts, now, runner=run_command, warn=None,
                  tail_bytes=DEFAULT_TAIL_BYTES):
    """Say each call the native side holds open once to every addressee, and once more when it has
    resumed. "Once" is read from the record the saying makes: the notes this watcher said, as folded
    in this device's channel store (`berth said`). Returns the number of failures."""
    warn = warn or (lambda line: print(line, file=sys.stderr))
    try:
        notes = berth_json(["said", "--session", ANNOUNCER, "--json"], runner)
    except (OSError, ValueError, RuntimeError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as error:
        warn(f"held-tool-watch: cannot read what was already said ({error}); nothing said this pass")
        return 1
    try:
        status = berth_json(["status", "--json"], runner)
    except (OSError, ValueError, RuntimeError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as error:
        warn(f"held-tool-watch: berth status unreadable ({error}); new lines go to the household")
        status = None
    device = status.get("device") if isinstance(status, dict) else None
    opened, resumed, fields = set(), set(), {}
    for note in notes if isinstance(notes, list) else []:
        parsed = parse_mark(note.get("text")) if isinstance(note, dict) else None
        if not parsed or not parsed[1].get("k"):
            continue
        kind, f = parsed
        target = (f["k"], note.get("to"))
        if kind == "open" and isinstance(note.get("at"), (int, float)) and note["at"] >= now - ANNOUNCE_LOOKBACK_S:
            opened.add(target)
            fields.setdefault(f["k"], f)
        elif kind == "resumed":
            resumed.add(target)

    def say(line, to):
        code, _, err = berth_run(["say", "--session", ANNOUNCER] + (["--to", to] if to else []) + [line],
                                 runner)
        if code != 0:
            warn(f"held-tool-watch: berth say failed (exit {code}): {' '.join(err.split())[:160] or 'no output'}")
            return 1
        return 0

    failed, current = 0, set()
    for h, binary in observed:
        key = announce_key(h)
        current.add(key)
        incidents = native_open_incidents(binary, h["session"], journal_root, runner)
        if incidents is None:
            warn(f"held-tool-watch: native status of session {h['session']} unreadable; not announced")
            failed += 1
            continue
        if not incidents:
            continue  # the native side holds nothing open: held state is the Incident, not this script
        if status is None and any(k == key for k, _ in opened):
            continue  # said already; whom else to tell is unknown this pass
        line = open_line(key, h, device, incidents[0], now)
        for to in addressees(status or {}, h["session"]):
            if (key, to) not in opened:
                failed += say(line, to)
    for key, f in sorted(fields.items()):
        if key in current or not all(f.get(x) for x in ("session", "agent", "call")):
            continue
        if still_pending(transcripts, f["session"], f["agent"], f["call"], tail_bytes) is not False:
            continue  # still pending, or unknown: never say resumed on a guess
        line = resumed_line(key, f, now)
        for k, to in sorted(opened, key=lambda kt: (kt[0], kt[1] or "")):
            if k == key and (k, to) not in resumed:
                failed += say(line, to)
    return failed


@contextlib.contextmanager
def file_lock(path, wait_s):
    """True once this process holds an exclusive lock on `path`, False when another holds it past
    wait_s (0 = one try). The lock orders writers; it records nothing."""
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o644)
    try:
        end = time.monotonic() + wait_s
        while True:
            try:
                fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
                break
            except BlockingIOError:
                if time.monotonic() >= end:
                    yield False
                    return
                time.sleep(0.2)
        yield True
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- CLI

def sensed(args):
    now = args.now if args.now is not None else time.time()
    sessions = moored_sessions(args.sessions_json)
    return scan(sessions, args.transcripts or transcripts_root(), args.sense_after_s, now,
                args.stasis_root or stasis_root(), args.tail_bytes)


def cmd_scan(args, runner=run_command):
    held = sensed(args)
    if args.json:
        print(json.dumps(held, sort_keys=True))
    else:
        for h in held:
            print(render_line(h))
    return 3 if held else 0


def cmd_observe(args, runner=run_command):
    held = sensed(args)
    if not held:
        return 0
    bin_store = args.bin_store or native_bin_store(runner)
    return 1 if observe_pass(held, args.stasis_root or stasis_root(), bin_store, runner) else 0


def cmd_announce(args, runner=run_command):
    now = args.now if args.now is not None else time.time()
    held = sensed(args)
    root = args.stasis_root or stasis_root()
    observed, failed = [], 0
    if held:
        failed = observe_pass(held, root, args.bin_store or native_bin_store(runner), runner, observed=observed)
    with file_lock(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(root), ANNOUNCE_LOCK), 30) as mine:
        if not mine:
            print("held-tool-watch: another announce pass holds the lock; this one said nothing",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        failed += announce_pass(observed, root, args.transcripts or transcripts_root(), now, runner,
                                tail_bytes=args.tail_bytes)
    return 1 if failed else 0


def cmd_run(args, runner=run_command):
    """The device runner: one per device (a lock beside the stasis root), one `announce` pass in a
    fresh process every --every seconds, so each pass runs the script's current bytes. It exits when
    its script is gone; the next hook in any session starts another."""
    root = args.stasis_root or stasis_root()
    script = os.path.realpath(__file__)
    passthrough = ["--sense-after-s", str(args.sense_after_s), "--tail-bytes", str(args.tail_bytes)]
    for flag, value in (("--transcripts", args.transcripts), ("--sessions-json", args.sessions_json),
                        ("--stasis-root", args.stasis_root), ("--bin-store", args.bin_store)):
        if value:
            passthrough += [flag, value]
    status_dir = os.path.dirname(root)
    with file_lock(os.path.join(status_dir, LOOP_LOCK), 0) as mine:
        if not mine:
            return 0  # this device already has its runner
        passes = 0
        while os.path.isfile(script):
            try:
                code, out, err = runner([sys.executable, script, "announce", *passthrough],
                                        timeout=max(60, 3 * args.every))
            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                code, out, err = None, "", "held-tool-watch: announce pass timed out\n"
            try:  # a diagnostic for a reader at the terminal, overwritten each pass; nothing decides on it
                with open(os.path.join(status_dir, LAST_PASS), "w") as f:
                    f.write(f"{rfc3339(time.time())} exit {code}\n{out[-4096:]}{err[-4096:]}")
            except OSError:
                pass
            passes += 1
            if args.passes and passes >= args.passes:
                break
            time.sleep(args.every)
    return 0


class _Parser(argparse.ArgumentParser):
    """A usage error is an internal error like any other: one line, exit 1 (argparse would exit 2)."""
    def error(self, message):
        raise ValueError(f"usage: {message}")


def parser():
    p = _Parser(prog="held-tool-watch", description=__doc__.strip().split("\n\n")[0])
    sub = p.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True, parser_class=_Parser)
    for name, run in (("scan", cmd_scan), ("observe", cmd_observe), ("announce", cmd_announce),
                      ("run", cmd_run)):
        s = sub.add_parser(name)
        s.add_argument("--transcripts")
        s.add_argument("--sense-after-s", type=float, default=120)
        s.add_argument("--sessions-json")
        s.add_argument("--stasis-root")
        s.add_argument("--tail-bytes", type=int, default=DEFAULT_TAIL_BYTES)
        if name != "run":
            s.add_argument("--now", type=float)
        if name == "scan":
            s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
        else:
            s.add_argument("--bin-store")
        if name == "run":
            s.add_argument("--every", type=float, default=60)
            s.add_argument("--passes", type=int, default=0)
        s.set_defaults(run=run)
    return p


def main(argv, runner=run_command):
    """Never raises: every failure is one stderr line and exit 1 (never 2, which a hook reads as a
    block). KeyboardInterrupt is a failure too."""
    try:
        p = parser()
        args = p.parse_args(argv)
        return args.run(args, runner=runner)
    except SystemExit as stop:  # --help
        return 0 if stop.code in (0, None) else 1
    except BaseException as error:  # noqa: BLE001 — the sensor's own failure must be a line, never silence
        print(f"held-tool-watch: {type(error).__name__}: {error}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
